# ---- 811 Manufacturing Engineering Technology I ----
H("811.d.1.A",3,"A new machinist must explain a delay to a shift supervisor in person and then document it for the purchasing office and a supplier in another country. She is demonstrating effective oral and written communication with:","individuals from varied backgrounds and roles",["only close friends","only family members","only people who agree"],"Different audiences need clear communication.")
H("811.d.1.A",4,"When writing to a supplier in another country, the clearest approach is to:","use plain, precise language and include measurements with units",["use slang and jokes","use only abbreviations","leave out dimensions"],"Plain precise language travels well.")
H("811.d.1.B",3,"A fabricator reads a print that shows a fillet weld symbol, a dimension callout and a section view before cutting any metal. He is interpreting:","engineering drawings, charts, diagrams and welding symbols",["a weather map","a seating chart","a recipe card"],"Prints tell how a part is built.")
H("811.d.1.B",4,"On an engineering drawing, a dimension callout tells the worker:","the size the feature must be made",["the color of the paint","the weight of the shipping box","the name of the buyer"],"Dimensions control size.")
H("811.d.1.C",3,"To drill a bolt circle of six equally spaced holes, a student uses geometry to find the angle between holes and algebra to find hole coordinates. She is selecting:","algebraic and geometric principles for precision measurement and calculation",["a music scale","a poem structure","a paint color"],"Math supports precision layout.")
H("811.d.1.C",4,"The angle between six equally spaced holes on a circle is:","60 degrees",["30 degrees","45 degrees","90 degrees"],"360 ÷ 6 = 60.")
H("811.d.2.A",3,"Before running a drill press, a student clamps the workpiece, ties back long hair and puts on safety glasses. He is using shop equipment:","in a safe manner",["in a hurry","without preparation","without guards"],"Safe setup prevents injuries.")
H("811.d.2.A",4,"The main reason to clamp a part before drilling is to:","keep it from spinning or lifting out of the vise",["make it heavier","make the hole bigger","speed the drill"],"Clamping prevents accidents.")
H("811.d.2.B",3,"A lathe has a chuck guard and a posted rule against wearing loose sleeves, while a grinder has a tool rest and a spark guard. Students are learning:","safety regulations for different types of manufacturing equipment",["office etiquette","menu design","music theory"],"Each machine has its own rules.")
H("811.d.2.B",4,"A rule that applies when working near rotating machinery is to avoid:","loose clothing, jewelry and dangling items",["safety glasses","a tied-back hairstyle","a clear work area"],"Loose items can catch.")
H("811.d.2.C",3,"A class turns a brass pin on a lathe, mills a flat on a block and welds two bars together following written procedures. They are executing procedures with:","different types of manufacturing equipment",["office software","kitchen appliances","garden tools"],"Procedures guide equipment use.")
H("811.d.2.C",4,"A machine that removes material by spinning a workpiece against a cutting tool is a:","lathe",["kiln","loom","printer"],"Lathes turn workpieces.")
H("811.d.2.D",3,"A class compares aluminum, stainless steel, carbon fiber and engineered plastics for strength, weight and cost before choosing a bracket material. They are researching:","modern materials used in manufacturing",["old recipes","folk songs","farm crops"],"Material choice drives design.")
H("811.d.2.D",4,"A reason engineers choose carbon fiber composites for some parts is:","a high strength-to-weight ratio",["very low cost","easy to melt","heavy mass"],"Strong yet light.")
H("811.d.2.E",3,"A technician measures a shaft with a micrometer to the nearest thousandth of an inch and records the reading. She is performing:","varied measurements, including precision measurements",["rough guesses","tasting tests","visual estimates only"],"Precision tools give accuracy.")
H("811.d.2.E",4,"A caliper is commonly used in a shop to measure:","outside and inside dimensions and depths",["temperature","humidity","sound level"],"Calipers measure lengths and depths.")
H("811.d.3.A",3,"A student presents a report on how additive manufacturing is used to print lightweight aircraft brackets. She is reporting on:","innovative applications of technology in engineering",["last year's sports scores","old fashions","a family recipe"],"Cutting-edge tech examples.")
H("811.d.3.A",4,"Another name for 3D printing in industry is:","additive manufacturing",["subtractive carving only","stamping only","casting only"],"Additive builds layer by layer.")
H("811.d.3.B",3,"A team tries a laser cutter on acrylic for the first time and compares the results with a handsaw to see how the new tool changes accuracy. They are:","experimenting with new technologies",["avoiding new tools","copying old methods","skipping tests"],"Experiments reveal what works.")
H("811.d.3.B",4,"When experimenting with a new tool, students should first:","read the safety information and test on scrap",["use it on the final part","skip training","ignore instructions"],"Test on scrap first.")
H("811.d.3.C",3,"A class forms identical coupons from plastic, fiberglass composite and wood, then tests how much load each can hold. They are experimenting with:","different manufacturing materials",["different pizza toppings","different shoe styles","different team colors"],"Compare materials by testing.")
H("811.d.3.C",4,"A composite material is made by:","combining two or more materials to gain properties neither has alone",["melting one metal","drying clay only","cutting wood only"],"Composites combine materials.")
H("811.d.4.A",3,"A team lists tasks, assigns people, sets milestones and checks results against the plan as they build a part. They are analyzing the processes of a project such as:","initiating, planning, executing, monitoring and closing",["sleeping, eating and playing","buying, selling and trading","starting, stopping and waiting"],"Project phases organize work.")
H("811.d.4.A",4,"The final phase of a project, in which the results are reviewed and lessons are recorded, is:","closing",["initiating","planning","executing"],"Closure wraps up.")
H("811.d.4.B",3,"A class sets up a drill press, a band saw and a sander to produce a bracket that meets the drawing's tolerance. They are using:","a variety of equipment and machines to produce an item to specification",["only hand tools","one tool only","no tools"],"Several machines meet specs.")
H("811.d.4.B",4,"A tolerance on a drawing tells the machinist:","how much a dimension is allowed to vary",["what color to paint","who ordered the part","how fast to cut"],"Tolerance = allowed variation.")
H("811.d.5.A",3,"A student earns a shop-safety certificate by passing a test based on federal workplace safety rules covering machine guards, protective gear and emergency procedures. She is mastering:","safety tests developed from OSHA guidelines and regulations",["a typing test","a geography quiz","a driving test"],"OSHA-based testing.")
H("811.d.5.A",4,"Protective gear such as safety glasses and hearing protection is called:","personal protective equipment (PPE)",["optional extras","decoration","toys"],"PPE protects workers.")
H("811.d.5.B",3,"A technician reads the label and safety data sheet on a cutting fluid and notes it is a skin irritant and must not be mixed with certain solvents. He is analyzing:","hazardous materials",["office supplies","lunch items","art supplies only"],"Read labels and sheets.")
H("811.d.5.B",4,"A safety data sheet is best used to find:","a chemical's hazards and safe handling",["the product price","the store location","the logo design"],"SDS explains hazards.")
H("811.d.5.C",3,"Used solvent rags are placed in a labeled, approved metal container rather than the regular trash. This shows how to:","dispose of hazardous materials safely",["hide waste","burn waste","pour waste outside"],"Proper disposal prevents fires.")
H("811.d.5.C",4,"Used oily rags are typically stored in:","an approved closed metal container",["a plastic bag in the sun","the regular trash","an open cardboard box"],"Prevents spontaneous combustion.")
H("811.d.5.D",3,"A shop stores flammable liquids in a labeled flammables cabinet away from welding sparks and keeps different chemicals separated. This is how to:","store all materials correctly",["store everything together","store in the open","store anywhere"],"Correct storage prevents accidents.")
H("811.d.5.D",4,"Flammable liquids should be stored:","in an approved flammables cabinet",["next to a heater","in open buckets","on the floor by the door"],"Use an approved cabinet.")
H("811.d.6.A",3,"A class forms a production line to make fifty identical key chains, with each student doing one step. They are participating in the manufacturing of:","a mass-produced project",["a one-off sculpture","a single prototype","a family photo"],"Mass production divides work.")
H("811.d.6.A",4,"A key advantage of dividing a task among a production line is:","consistent work done faster",["slower output","lower quality","random results"],"Specialization speeds work.")
H("811.d.6.B",3,"A student measures every tenth key chain with a gauge and records the results on a chart to catch any drift from the target size. She is developing a method to:","check and maintain quality control throughout manufacturing",["decorate parts","hide errors","skip inspection"],"Sampling checks quality.")
H("811.d.6.B",4,"Inspecting a sample of parts from a production run is a way to:","catch problems before many bad parts are made",["make parts heavier","avoid testing","increase defects"],"Sampling prevents waste.")
H("811.d.7.A",3,"A team totals the cost of material, labor and tool wear for a batch of brackets and compares it with the selling price. They are developing a:","budget for a project",["travel brochure","party invitation","playlist"],"Budgets plan costs.")
H("811.d.7.A",4,"Before starting a class manufacturing run, a team compares what the materials and labor will cost against the funds the program has. This comparison is the core of a:","project budget",["parts diagram","safety poster","shipping label"],"A budget matches expected costs to available funds.")
H("811.d.7.B",3,"A class finds that nesting parts on one sheet of steel wastes less material than cutting from many sheets. They are determining:","the most effective strategies to minimize costs",["a way to raise prices only","a way to waste more","a way to avoid planning"],"Reduce waste to cut costs.")
H("811.d.7.B",4,"One way a plant lowers cost per part is by:","reducing scrap and rework",["adding defects","using more material","slowing the line"],"Less waste, lower cost.")
H("811.d.8.A",3,"A student team writes a plan for selling their key chains that names the buyer, the price, where to advertise and a launch date. They are preparing:","a marketing plan for a product",["a seating chart","a lunch menu","a game roster"],"Marketing plans promote products.")
H("811.d.8.A",4,"A marketing plan should identify:","the target customers and how to reach them",["only the product color","only the cost of paint","only the factory name"],"Know your audience.")
H("811.d.8.B",3,"After several customers return a product because it breaks easily, sales drop and online reviews turn negative. Students are analyzing the effect of:","customer satisfaction on the image of a product",["weather on traffic","music on homework","sports on health"],"Satisfaction shapes reputation.")
H("811.d.8.B",4,"Happy customers are most likely to:","recommend the product and buy again",["return everything","avoid the brand","post complaints"],"Loyalty follows satisfaction.")
H("811.d.8.C",3,"Survey results show buyers want a lighter, rechargeable flashlight, so the design team changes the housing and battery. They are analyzing how:","customer demands influence the design of an object",["fog affects visibility","price tags affect color","sunlight affects sleep"],"Design follows demand.")
H("811.d.8.C",4,"When customers repeatedly ask for a feature, a company often:","redesigns the product to include it",["ignores the request","raises price only","stops selling"],"Demand drives design.")
H("811.d.9.A",3,"During a team meeting, a lead tells the crew the order of operations, the tolerances and the inspection points in plain terms and asks each member to repeat it back. She is demonstrating:","communication techniques consistent with industry standards",["rumor-passing","guesswork","silence"],"Standard communication prevents mistakes.")
H("811.d.9.A",4,"A shift handoff note on a machine should include:","the job status, problems and next steps",["jokes","opinions about coworkers","unrelated stories"],"Handoffs pass key info.")
H("811.d.9.B",3,"A machinist cannot remember the correct feed rate for stainless steel, so she checks a machinist's handbook and the tool maker's catalog. She is:","locating relevant information needed to solve problems",["guessing","skipping the job","asking a stranger"],"Reference materials give data.")
H("811.d.9.B",4,"A machinist's handbook is a reliable source for:","speeds, feeds and standard dimensions",["sports scores","celebrity news","menus"],"Handbooks give shop data.")
H("811.d.9.C",3,"To cut a 3.5-meter pipe into four equal sections, a worker divides the length and marks each cut. He is applying:","mathematics concepts to solve manufacturing problems",["music theory","dance steps","cooking skills"],"Division finds equal lengths.")
H("811.d.9.C",4,"Each of four equal sections cut from a 3.5-meter pipe is:","0.875 meters",["1.0 meters","0.75 meters","1.25 meters"],"3.5 ÷ 4 = 0.875.")
H("811.d.9.D",3,"A technician explains that a heated steel rod grows slightly longer because its particles move farther apart, so the shop leaves expansion gaps in long rails. She is analyzing:","science principles used to solve problems",["fashion trends","sports history","travel plans"],"Thermal expansion matters.")
H("811.d.9.D",4,"Most metals, when heated, will:","expand",["shrink","turn to powder","disappear"],"Thermal expansion.")
H("811.d.9.E",3,"A purchasing clerk checks that the order lists the pipe length in meters and the diameter in millimeters to match the shop's drawings. She is using:","appropriate units of measure",["random units","no units","mixed units"],"Consistent units prevent errors.")
H("811.d.9.E",4,"The SI base unit of length is the:","meter",["yard","foot","mile"],"Meter is the SI unit of length.")

# ---- 812 Manufacturing Engineering Technology II ----
H("812.d.1.A",3,"A second-year technician leads a briefing for a crew, then emails a written work order to the client's engineer and a vendor overseas. She is demonstrating effective oral and written communication with:","individuals from varied roles and backgrounds",["only the crew","only classmates","only her friends"],"Audiences differ; messages must fit.")
H("812.d.1.A",4,"A written work order sent to an outside vendor should be:","clear, complete and specific about requirements",["vague and brief","full of slang","written without dates"],"Clarity prevents errors.")
H("812.d.1.B",3,"A welder checks the arrow side of a weld symbol, the weld size and the field-weld flag on a drawing before striking an arc. She is interpreting:","engineering drawings, charts, diagrams and welding symbols",["a movie script","a seating map","a grocery receipt"],"Symbols specify the weld.")
H("812.d.1.B",4,"On a welding symbol, the reference line, the arrow and the tail together tell the welder:","what weld to make, where and how",["who the customer is","which break room to use","when lunch starts"],"Symbol anatomy gives instructions.")
H("812.d.1.C",3,"A machinist calculates the diagonal of a rectangular plate with the Pythagorean theorem to check that a part will fit a fixture. He is selecting:","algebraic and geometric principles required for precision measurement and calculation",["a poem form","a music chord","a recipe ratio"],"Geometry supports fit-checks.")
H("812.d.1.C",4,"A rectangular plate is 3 inches by 4 inches. Its diagonal is:","5 inches",["6 inches","7 inches","12 inches"],"3-4-5 right triangle.")
H("812.d.1.D",3,"Before ordering 500 identical brackets, a team draws a flow chart of each operation, lists the materials and times each step. They are developing the information needed to:","mass produce a simple project",["bake cookies","plan a trip","write a song"],"Process planning supports mass production.")
H("812.d.1.D",4,"A flow process chart is useful in mass production because it:","shows the sequence of steps and where delays occur",["lists the team's hobbies","shows the weather","hides the process"],"Charts reveal the sequence.")
H("812.d.1.E",3,"A shop builds a block with locating pins so each bracket can be clamped in exactly the same place for drilling every time. The class is exploring the use of:","jigs and fixtures in mass production",["paint cans","ladders","extension cords"],"Jigs and fixtures hold and guide work.")
H("812.d.1.E",4,"A jig differs from a fixture because it:","guides the cutting tool as well as holding the part",["is only decoration","has no purpose","cannot hold parts"],"Jigs guide tools.")
H("812.d.2.A",3,"A student sets the guard, secures the workpiece and checks that the sander's emergency stop works before turning it on. She is using shop tools and equipment:","in a safe manner",["without checks","carelessly","in a hurry"],"Safe use starts with checks.")
H("812.d.2.A",4,"Before starting any machine, a student should confirm:","the guards are in place and the emergency stop works",["the music is on","the room is warm","the clock is right"],"Pre-use checks.")
H("812.d.2.B",3,"A grinder operator always keeps the tool rest within an eighth inch of the wheel and never removes the wheel guard. She is adhering to:","safety regulations for different types of manufacturing equipment",["classroom decor rules","playground rules","cafeteria rules"],"Equipment rules prevent injuries.")
H("812.d.2.B",4,"If a safety guard on a machine is missing, the correct action is to:","stop and report it before using the machine",["use the machine carefully","remove other guards","ignore it"],"Report missing guards.")
H("812.d.2.C",3,"A team follows the written setup sheet to run a CNC lathe, mill a keyway on a milling machine and weld a frame. They are executing procedures with:","different types of manufacturing equipment",["different musical instruments","different vehicles","different sports gear"],"Procedures guide each machine.")
H("812.d.2.C",4,"A setup sheet for a machine typically lists:","tools, speeds, feeds and the order of operations",["jokes","party plans","lunch orders"],"Setup sheets guide operations.")
H("812.d.2.D",3,"A quality inspector checks a hole's diameter with a bore gauge and a flatness with a dial indicator. She is performing:","varied measurements, including precision measurements",["rough estimates","visual guesses","taste checks"],"Different gauges for different features.")
H("812.d.2.D",4,"A dial indicator is mostly used to measure:","small variations such as runout and flatness",["room temperature","weight","volume of liquids"],"Indicators detect tiny variation.")
H("812.d.2.E",3,"A student designs a drilling jig with two bushings and a clamp plate for a bracket with three holes and a flat base. She is designing and developing:","jigs and fixtures for a simple product of four or fewer parts",["a poster","a toy only","a lunch plan"],"Design jigs for the product.")
H("812.d.2.E",4,"A drill bushing in a jig helps to:","guide the drill so holes land in the right place",["heat the part","paint the part","sort the parts"],"Bushings guide drills.")
H("812.d.2.F",3,"On run-off day, the class sets up stations, divides the steps and builds one hundred brackets using the jigs. They are participating in:","the production run of the product",["a lecture","a field trip","a quiz"],"Run-off puts the plan into action.")
H("812.d.2.F",4,"During a production run, the main benefit of jigs and fixtures is:","consistent parts from one piece to the next",["more variation","slower work","more scrap"],"Repeatability.")
H("812.d.3.A",3,"A student draws a part in software, then uses a program to generate tool paths and code for a mill. She is developing:","a CNC program using a computer-aided manufacturing (CAM) program",["a hand drawing","a quilt pattern","a song"],"CAM creates tool paths.")
H("812.d.3.A",4,"CAM software is used to:","create tool paths and machine instructions from a design",["compose music","write novels","edit photos"],"CAM = computer-aided manufacturing.")
H("812.d.3.B",3,"Before cutting aluminum, a student runs the CNC program in simulation mode to see whether the tool crashes into the clamps. She is:","executing the CNC program to machine a product or run a simulation",["skipping verification","deleting the file","guessing"],"Simulations catch errors.")
H("812.d.3.B",4,"A major reason to simulate a CNC program before cutting is to:","catch collisions and errors without damaging parts",["make it louder","slow production","avoid learning"],"Simulation saves parts and tools.")
H("812.d.4.A",3,"A student investigates how robotic welding cells and additive manufacturing are changing factories and writes a summary. She is researching:","innovative technologies in manufacturing",["last year's fashion","local weather","pop songs"],"Explore current innovation.")
H("812.d.4.A",4,"Collaborative robots, or cobots, are designed to:","work safely alongside humans in a shared space",["replace all factories","work only in the dark","operate without any controls"],"Cobots share workspaces.")
H("812.d.4.B",3,"A class tests how nylon, aluminum and a glass-filled composite hold up after repeated bending to choose the best clip material. They are experimenting with:","different manufacturing materials",["different snacks","different games","different hats"],"Experiments guide material selection.")
H("812.d.4.B",4,"When comparing materials for a part, an engineer first considers:","the properties the part needs, such as strength and weight",["the brand's logo","the color of the package","the day of the week"],"Match properties to needs.")
H("812.d.5.A",3,"A team studies how stress, strength and stiffness of a beam depend on the material and its shape before choosing a design. They are analyzing:","engineering properties of materials and designs",["weather forecasts","playground games","cooking times"],"Properties guide design.")
H("812.d.5.A",4,"A material that returns to its original shape after a load is removed is said to be:","elastic",["brittle only","liquid","gaseous"],"Elastic recovers shape.")
H("812.d.5.B",3,"A class writes a project plan with a charter, schedule, tasks, checkpoints and a final review for their production run. They are analyzing the processes of a project such as:","initiating, planning, executing, monitoring and closing",["eating, resting and sleeping","buying, saving and spending","starting, drifting and quitting"],"Project phases.")
H("812.d.5.B",4,"In the monitoring phase of a project, the team:","checks progress against the plan and adjusts",["finishes the plan","never reviews work","ignores problems"],"Monitor and control.")
H("812.d.5.C",3,"A team selects from calipers, a mill, a drill press and a deburring tool to produce a part to the print's tolerance. They are using:","a variety of tools and equipment to produce a product to specification",["only one tool","no tools","a single guess"],"Right tools meet specs.")
H("812.d.5.C",4,"A part is made 'to specification' when it:","meets all the dimensions and tolerances on the print",["looks good","is heavy","is colorful"],"Specs define acceptance.")
H("812.d.6.A",3,"To work in the shop, a student must pass an exam on machine guarding, lockout/tagout, PPE and hazard communication rooted in federal workplace rules. She is mastering:","safety tests based on OSHA regulations",["a typing test","a spelling quiz","a trivia game"],"OSHA-based training.")
H("812.d.6.A",4,"Lockout/tagout procedures are used to:","keep a machine from starting during maintenance",["speed production","decorate a shop","paint the floor"],"LOTO protects workers.")
H("812.d.6.B",3,"A technician reads the safety data sheet on a degreaser to learn its flash point, required gloves and first-aid steps. She is analyzing:","hazardous materials",["pizza toppings","playground gear","school posters"],"SDS details hazards.")
H("812.d.6.B",4,"A flash point tells a worker:","the lowest temperature at which a liquid gives off ignitable vapors",["the boiling price","the pour speed","the color intensity"],"Flash point = ignition risk.")
H("812.d.6.C",3,"Waste coolant is collected in a labeled drum and picked up by an authorized hauler instead of being poured down a drain. This demonstrates how to:","dispose of hazardous materials properly",["hide waste","dump in a ditch","burn it"],"Proper disposal protects the environment.")
H("812.d.6.C",4,"Used coolant and oils should be:","collected and disposed of through an approved process",["poured outside","burned in a barrel","buried in the yard"],"Approved disposal only.")
H("812.d.6.D",3,"Compressed gas cylinders are chained upright, capped when not in use and stored away from flammables. This shows how to:","store all materials safely",["store them loosely","store them near heat","store them in a pile"],"Proper storage prevents accidents.")
H("812.d.6.D",4,"A welding shop keeps two full oxygen tanks near its torch cart. Which storage practice is correct?","chain them upright and keep the valve caps on",["lay them flat on the floor","lean them against a wall unsecured","remove the caps for quick access"],"Secured upright cylinders with caps are safest.")
H("812.d.7.A",3,"Following the process chart, students operate each station to make a batch of identical parts to the plan. They are participating in:","the manufacturing of products",["a rehearsal for a play","a spelling bee","a bake sale"],"Production applies the plan.")
H("812.d.7.A",4,"In a production setting, each worker at a station is responsible for:","completing a specific step to the standard",["inventing a new step","skipping steps","changing tolerances"],"Stations have defined duties.")
H("812.d.7.B",3,"A team uses a control chart to plot the diameter of a sample of parts every fifteen minutes and flags any drift outside the limits. They are developing:","a method to check and maintain quality control",["a decorating plan","a seating plan","a pricing plan"],"Control charts track quality.")
H("812.d.7.B",4,"A control limit on a quality chart shows:","the range within which the process is considered stable",["the best price","the customer count","the shop temperature"],"Limits flag instability.")
H("812.d.8.A",3,"A student totals the cost of raw stock, machine time, labor and tooling and divides by the number of parts to find the cost per part. She is calculating:","costs associated with production of a mass-produced product",["a sports score","a grade average","a travel distance"],"Cost per part.")
H("812.d.8.A",4,"If a batch of 200 parts costs $1,000 to produce, the cost per part is:","$5",["$2","$10","$20"],"1000 ÷ 200 = 5.")
H("812.d.8.B",3,"A team reorders the stations to cut the walking distance between operations and finds they can save time on every part. They are:","re-examining the manufacturing process to maximize efficiency and minimize costs",["adding delays","ignoring waste","raising costs"],"Process improvement.")
H("812.d.8.B",4,"Reducing unnecessary motion and waiting in a process is a way to:","improve efficiency and lower costs",["increase waste","slow output","raise defects"],"Efficiency lowers cost.")
H("812.d.9.A",3,"A student group writes a marketing plan for an engraved cutting board, listing target buyers, price, a sales channel and promotion ideas. They are preparing:","a marketing plan for a product",["a game schedule","a cafeteria menu","a class roster"],"Marketing plans promote products.")
H("812.d.9.A",4,"The price in a marketing plan is set so that it:","covers costs and is acceptable to the target customers",["is as low as possible","is as high as possible","is random"],"Price balances cost and value.")
H("812.d.9.B",3,"After several buyers post reviews that the handles loosen quickly, repeat orders drop and the brand's reputation suffers. Students are analyzing:","the effect of customer satisfaction on a product's image",["the effect of rain on grass","the effect of music on sleep","the effect of food on mood"],"Satisfaction affects image.")
H("812.d.9.B",4,"A company can protect its image by:","fixing defects and responding to customer feedback",["ignoring complaints","hiding problems","raising prices only"],"Respond to feedback.")
H("812.d.9.C",3,"Buyers say a toolbox is too heavy and hard to carry, so engineers redesign it with lighter material and a better handle. They are analyzing how:","customer demands influence the design of an object",["rain affects roads","sunlight affects plants","sleep affects mood"],"Design follows demand.")
H("812.d.9.C",4,"Customer feedback surveys help designers by:","showing what features customers want",["hiding problems","increasing cost only","replacing testing"],"Feedback guides design.")
H("812.d.10.A",3,"The shift lead uses a standard handoff form and verbally reviews each open job with the incoming lead before leaving. She is demonstrating:","communication techniques consistent with industry standards",["rumor-passing","silence","guessing"],"Handoff standards prevent errors.")
H("812.d.10.A",4,"A good handoff between shifts includes:","a clear summary of status, issues and what is next",["only the weather","only gossip","nothing"],"Clear handoffs.")
H("812.d.10.B",3,"Unsure how to program a thread cut, a student checks the machine's programming manual and the tool vendor's data sheet. She is:","locating relevant information needed to solve problems",["guessing","quitting","ignoring the problem"],"Find authoritative info.")
H("812.d.10.B",4,"A tool vendor's data sheet is a good source for:","recommended speeds, feeds and materials for a tool",["sports news","weather","music reviews"],"Vendor data guides use.")
H("812.d.10.C",3,"A planner must figure how many 8-inch parts can be cut from a 20-foot bar with each cut wasting a quarter inch. She is applying:","mathematics concepts to solve manufacturing problems",["cooking math only","sports stats","calendar dates"],"Applied arithmetic.")
